      "baseRefName": "main",
      "body": "GeoImpact CI V5 can support a standalone static review surface, but the requested two-case viewer remains on HOLD: the Madrid source register explicitly leaves INE redistribution conditions unresolved. The official collection footer and general legal notice still expose differing license labels. Following the requested stop rule, this experiment delivers design and a reproducible technical proof without implementing or presenting a finished viewer.\n\nAll ten additions are confined to `experiments/review-studio/`:\n\n- Evidence-backed audit of released v1.2.0, V5, actual regenerated outputs, source rights and existing features; eight proposed architecture decisions.\n- Desktop, tablet and mobile SVG designs, explicitly labelled as designs rather than screenshots, with ES/EN copy and measurable J1–J5 acceptance criteria.\n- Standard-library display-readiness probe, retained metadata summary and eight failure-mode tests. No spatial predicates, metric computation or policy execution are introduced.\n- Reproduction instructions, professional utility/risk assessment and exact criteria for reopening implementation.\n\nValidation completed locally on Linux/Python 3.12.14: released suite 113 passed; existing experiment-branch suite 113 passed; eight probe tests passed; PASS/BLOCK/ERROR contracts and synthetic hashes matched; Madrid and Sierra existing verifiers passed with all six frozen output hashes. Original inputs and evidence join successfully by declared IDs. SVGs were locally rasterized and inspected.\n\nNo functional UI, browser viewport tests, physical-device tests, UI screenshots or human user research are claimed. These remain explicit later gates. No source geometry is duplicated into a web bundle. CLI, algorithms, policies, deterministic serialization, reference fixtures, public contracts, dependencies, packaging and existing CI remain untouched. No merge or deployment.\n\nStart at [the experiment README](https://github.com/soroushkarahrodi79-oss/geoimpact-ci/blob/experiment/review-studio-feasibility/experiments/review-studio/README.md). R1 requires retained authoritative dataset-specific reuse evidence for the exact INE snapshots and their derived display/redistribution; inclusion in this repository and attribution alone do not close that recorded ambiguity.",
